  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nGiven `<form target=_blank>` and `<a target=_blank>`, https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/links.html#get-an-element's-noopener says that we should treat that as noopener. This was raised back in https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/7256 with changes to tests that used that pattern to add `rel=opener`, with the promise that implementations would change to match the spec.\n\nBehold https://wpt.fyi/results/html/browsers/the-window-object/open-close/script-closable.html?label=experimental&label=master&aligned, which uses this same pattern in 2026 and all engines pass the tests:\n* https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/9b4775eac18993ffc6216d71b5c773bdb9695f09/html/browsers/the-window-object/open-close/script-closable.html#L34-L38\n* https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/9b4775eac18993ffc6216d71b5c773bdb9695f09/html/browsers/the-window-object/open-close/script-closable.html#L59-L62",
